# Road posts: the speaker at the barrier (Dialogue > Trees puts one there while a player is within
# 100 m). The crew stays an AI group. Search and toll are the built ones.

# Who's at the barrier, said once to someone the post doesn't know: the post's speaker has no greeting
# line of its own on the talk screen (the hub opens on the replies), so the first meeting carries it.
conv post.bastion.hello
for post:bastion
when !hunted:bastion & !kit:in_kit
greet
prio flavour
once
voice bastion

node start
  say? !met :: This is Task Force Bastion's checkpoint at {here}. We were left inside when the Zone was sealed, and we hold this road for our own. You're not one of ours, so it's the pole and a search.

conv post.redhand.hello
for post:redhand
when !hunted:redhand & !kit:in_kit
greet
prio flavour
once
voice redhand

node start
  say? !met :: This road's the Red Hand's, from the lorry to the bend, and I'm the one who takes the toll. Nobody's coming to fix the Zone, so we charge for using it. Talk nicely and you get a price.

conv post.bastion.search
for post:bastion
when !hunted:bastion
topic "What's the search for?"
prio world
voice bastion

node start
  say Every civilian through this barrier gets searched. Hands on the pole, pockets out, and it's fifteen seconds if you don't argue. Twenty if you do.
  say We take suppressors and explosives and nothing else. Your food, your meds, your rifle, you keep. Walk off before we're done and you've run a Bastion checkpoint, and that goes in the log.
  > @drill I've stood at a barrier. Make it quick. -> waved | short | refused   check persuade bastion 2 bg:soldier,police
  > @why Why search civilians at all? -> why
  > @fine Fine. Hands on the pole. Go ahead. -> hub

node waved
  say You've stood on this side of a pole before. Hands where I'd want them before I asked. Go on through, and keep to the left of the road past the sandbags.
  do call:post_wave
  > @thanks Thanks, corporal. -> hub

node short
  say Quick I can do. Skipping it I can't, not with the sergeant watching from the hut. Arms out, and I'll make it ten seconds instead of fifteen.
  > @ok Arms out. Go on. -> hub

node refused
  say Everyone who walks up this road says they know the drill. The ones who really do don't say it. Hands on the pole, same as everyone, and you'll be through.
  > @ok2 Fair enough. Go ahead. -> hub

node why
  say Somebody walked up to a post in the north with a smile and a charge under his coat. Two of that gate crew are tags on the nail behind the radio now. Since then, everyone gets searched.
  say Especially the ones we like. They're the ones who get close enough to matter.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv post.redhand.toll
for post:redhand
when !hunted:redhand
topic "What's the toll here?"
prio world
voice redhand

node start
  say Red hand means stop. Stop means pay. This stretch is ours from the lorry to the bend, and for you, today, the toll is {toll} Favor. It goes in the book with your face next to it.
  say Or you walk round through the fields. It's only a few kilometres, and the people out there are mostly dead. They don't charge. They do bite.
  > @pay Fine. Here's your {toll} Favor. -> paid   if tier:redhand>=known   do call:toll
  > @move Move the lorry, or I move you. -> moved | laughed | laughed   check threaten redhand 2
  > @rudi This was Rudi's road once, wasn't it? -> rudi
  > @sent Rudi sent me. -> waved | rudi_lie   check lie redhand 2   tell always
  > @walk I'll take the fields, thanks. -> hub

node waved
  say Did he, now. Well, then. Off you pop, and don't let the lorry see you smile.
  > @back4 Right. Something else, then. -> hub

node rudi_lie
  say Nice try. Everyone on this road knows that name, and nobody sends anybody anywhere in it. The toll's still {toll}.
  say Rudi was bitten.
  > @pay3 Fine. Here's your {toll} Favor. -> paid   if tier:redhand>=known   do call:toll
  > @round2 I'll go round by the fields. -> hub

node paid
  say Pleasure doing business. That's you in the book, paid, today's date. Mind the bend past the lorry: we leave the dead where they drop, and they don't always stay dropped.
  > @back1 I'll mind it. One more thing. -> hub

node moved
  say Fine. Fine! Lads, shift the lorry, this one's got a face on. And somebody write it in the book: waved through, owes us a fright.
  do call:post_wave
  > @back2 Good. Now, something else. -> hub

node laughed
  say Look at that, lads, a hard face. Lovely. There are six of us and a shotgun on the cab, so it still costs {toll}, and now the book's got your face in it twice.
  > @pay2 Fine. Here's your {toll} Favor. -> paid   if tier:redhand>=known   do call:toll
  > @round Keep your lorry. I'll walk round. -> hub

node rudi
  say This was a garage forecourt and a crossroads before it was a toll. The shutter you walked past, the one we paint the hand on, was Rudi's.
  say Rudi was bitten.
  > @back3 Right. Let me ask about something else. -> hub
